From: John Drummond <john.drummond@ultra-sss.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Background layer: rebuild drawables after the layer tweaker is replaced

A style switch that keeps the layer id (Liberty <-> Positron) calls layerChanged, which detaches the tweaker.
The existing drawables kept pointing at the old tweaker (stale properties); only a pan/zoom that changed the
tile cover rebuilt them. Remove drawables whose tweaker is not the current one so they are rebuilt.

diff --git a/src/mln/renderer/layers/render_background_layer.cpp b/src/mln/renderer/layers/render_background_layer.cpp
--- a/src/mln/renderer/layers/render_background_layer.cpp
+++ b/src/mln/renderer/layers/render_background_layer.cpp
@@ -206,8 +206,12 @@
 
     // Remove drawables for tiles that are no longer in the cover set.
     // (Note that `RenderTiles` is empty, and this layer does not use it)
+    // Also remove drawables made for a previous tweaker: `layerChanged` (a style switch that keeps the layer id)
+    // detaches the tweaker, and a drawable still pointing at the old one would keep stale properties and
+    // projection state, because only its own tweaker updates it.
     tileLayerGroup->removeDrawablesIf([&](gfx::Drawable& drawable) -> bool {
-        return drawable.getTileID() && (std::ranges::find(tileCover, *drawable.getTileID()) == tileCover.end());
+        return drawable.getTileID() && (drawable.getLayerTweaker() != layerTweaker ||
+                                        std::ranges::find(tileCover, *drawable.getTileID()) == tileCover.end());
     });
 
     // For each tile in the cover set, add a tile drawable if one doesn't already exist.
